                return False
    return not stack
```
The `check_expression` function uses a stack to traverse through each character of the expression. If an opening bracket is encountered, it is pushed onto the stack. If a closing bracket is encountered, the function checks if the stack is empty or if the top of the stack does not correspond to the matching opening bracket. If any of these conditions are not met, the function returns `False`, indicating that the expression is not balanced. If the stack is empty at the end of the traversal, it means that every opening bracket had a corresponding closing bracket, and the expression is balanced, so the function returns `True`.

