            x[i][j] = x[i - 1][j] + x[i][j - 1]

    return x[n][m]
```

This Python function implements the recursive approach to calculate the Lobb number, which is also known as the "Catalan number". The function initializes a 2D array with the dimensions based on the input values `n` and `m`, setting the values for the first row and first column. Then, it uses dynamic programming to fill in the rest of the array based on the recurrence relation: `x[i][j] = x[i-1][j] + x[i][j-1]`. Finally, it returns the value at `x[n][m]` which represents the Lobb number for the given values of `n` and `m`.

