    length = len(triangle)
    for i in range(1, length):
        for j in range(i + 1):
            triangle[i][j] += min(triangle[i - 1][j], triangle[i - 1][j + 1])
    return min(triangle[-1])
```

The function `min_sum_path` iterates through the triangle from the second row to the top. For each element, it updates the value to be the sum of itself and the minimum of the two directly below it in the triangle. After completing the iteration, it returns the minimum value in the top row, which represents the minimum path sum to reach the bottom of the triangle.

