def min_sum_path(triangle):
    if not triangle:
        return 0

    # Start from the second row and move upwards
    for row in range(1, len(triangle)):
        for col in range(len(triangle[row])):
            # Add the minimum of the two adjacent numbers from the row below
            triangle[row][col] += min(triangle[row-1][col],triangle[row-1][col+1])

    # The top element will now contain the minimum total path sum
    return triangle[-1][0]
```

This function iterates through the triangle from the second row upwards. For each element, it updates the element to be the sum of itself and the minimum of its two adjacent elements from the row below. After processing all elements, the top element of the triangle will contain the minimum total path sum.

