This function `are_Equal` takes four parameters: `arr1`, `arr2`, `len1`, and `len2`, which represent the two arrays and the lengths of those arrays, respectively. It first checks if the lengths of the arrays are equal. If not, it immediately returns `False`. If the lengths are equal, it then iterates through the arrays, comparing each element at each position. If any pair of elements does not match, it returns `False`. If the loop completes without finding any mismatches, it means the arrays are equal, so the function returns `True`.
